statement:
Fix the finite-field datum [def-weil-finite-field-fiber] $p,a,q,k_0,k$, a prime $\ell\neq p$, an algebraic closure $\Qlb$ of $\Ql$, a finite-type [def-weil-scheme-morphism-properties] $k_0$-scheme $Y_0$, $Y=Y_0\times_{k_0}k$ and the geometric Frobenius $g_Y$ [def-weil-frobenius-detailed]. For every finite extension $E/\Ql$ inside $\Qlb$ let $(E_Y,\theta_E)\in D^b_{c,\mathrm W}(Y,E)$ be the canonical Weil structure of [def-weil-constant-weil-structure]. Then for finite extensions $E\subset L$ inside $\Qlb$:

1. the canonical isomorphism $\alpha_{E,L}:E_Y\otimes_EL\xrightarrow{\sim}L_Y$ in $D^b_c(Y,L)$ of [lem-weil-constant-coefficient-objects-constructible] (scalar extension of [def-weil-rationalization-karoubi]) satisfies $\theta_L\circ Lg_Y^*(\alpha_{E,L})=\alpha_{E,L}\circ(\theta_E\otimes_EL)$, where $Lg_Y^*(E_Y\otimes_EL)$ is identified with $(Lg_Y^*E_Y)\otimes_EL$ by the compatibility of the derived pullback [def-weil-derived-pullback-tensor-hom] with scalar extension; so $\alpha_{E,L}$ is an isomorphism $(E_Y,\theta_E)\otimes_EL\cong(L_Y,\theta_L)$ of $L$-Weil sheaves [def-weil-weil-sheaf-complex];
2. consequently, in the common-stage category $D^b_{c,\mathrm W}(Y,\Qlb)$ [def-weil-weil-sheaf-complex, def-weil-algebraically-closed-coefficients], the object $(E,(E_Y,\theta_E))$ is canonically isomorphic to the canonical Weil structure $(\Ql,((\Ql)_Y,\theta_{\Ql}))$ on $(\Qlb)_Y$, compatibly with the forgetful functor $\operatorname{For}$.
